WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.908
What if humanity grew to
be so technologically advanced

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.177
that we were able to leave our Solar System

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.480
and spread across interstellar space?

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.294
This is WHAT IF,

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.562
and here's what would happen

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.232
if humanity became an interstellar society.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.437
No human has ever been
outside of our Solar System,

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.273
and only a few of us have
actually left the Earth.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:44.277
Even those who blasted out of
here in a rocket didn't go too far.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:47.247
There are billions upon
billions of planets out there.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:51.584
But they are so far away, it would
take us a very long time to reach them.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.320
If we jumped into the
fastest spacecraft ever built,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.823
it would take us over 70,000 years

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.793
to get to our neighboring
star system Alpha Centauri.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:05.198
Even if we could accelerate a
spaceship to 99% the speed of light,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:10.703
over 26,000 years would pass until we
arrived at the center of our own galaxy.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.173
And another 2 million years until we set foot

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.776
in the nearest neighbor,
the Andromeda galaxy.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:20.180
How could we go about expanding
our civilization into space

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.215
if we're so terribly slow?

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.052
To become an intergalactic civilization,

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.922
we'd need to break the
speed limit of the Universe.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.425
But for all we know, traveling at the
lightspeed is physically impossible,

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.928
nevermind outperforming it.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.863
The Universe is enormous,

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.364
possibly infinite.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.469
And our lifespans are too miserably
short to cover those kind of distances

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.670
even at near-light speeds.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.674
But let your curiosity take over

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.642
and imagine we were a civilization

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:53.146
that could approach lightspeed
and travel among stars.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:57.784
We'd start with Alpha Centauri,
our neighboring star system.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:01.821
Who knows - maybe the exoplanet
orbiting this three-star system

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.857
would turn out to be habitable.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.626
Then, we'd push ourselves out further

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.362
to discover the billions of other worlds. 

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.998
Not all of them would be
suitable for us to settle in.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.069
In astronomy, a habitable world is a planet

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.038
that is just the right distance
from its Sun-like star

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.908
to be able to sustain liquid water.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.945
But the reality is, humans
require so much more than that.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:29.716
Atmosphere, gravity, temperature -
they're all important.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.953
It's unlikely that we'd find
another planet just like Earth.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:38.324
But we could build self-sustaining
Earth-like biomes on our giant spaceships,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.560
where humans could live for generations.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:45.165
Or, we could terraform some rocky exoplanets.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.601
First, we'd harvest water
from a few ice comets.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.272
Then, we'd alter the planets'
atmospheres to resemble Earth's.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.941
Anything to be able to
breathe in fresh air again.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.244
Even though space would be so accessible,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.113
people wouldn't travel
around the Universe much

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.348
once the new colonies were established.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.783
Even at the speed of light,

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:07.453
it would take generations to make a
trip to the other side of the Universe.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.323
Space is just too vast, remember?

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.459
In this new world, you'd
get to travel among stars

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.461
only if you were a part of a ship's crew,

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.863
a colonist,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.997
or a space miner.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:22.702
We'd send robots to perform
our intergalactic chores.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.638
Robots don't eat, sleep,
or go to the bathroom.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.409
They can withstand high levels of
radiation and extreme temperatures -

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:32.378
all the things that would
kill a human being.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.647
But if space travel is something you crave,

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:37.951
consider pursuing a
career as a postal carrier.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.353
Because the most reliable
way to communicate

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.155
might be through the mail.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.256
Surprised?

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:47.594
Well, our satellites rely on radio
waves to transmit information.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.630
Even though these waves
travel just as fast as light,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.032
they lose their strength over long distances.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:56.836
It's like being too far away
from your WiFi router.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.772
If humanity did become an interstellar society,

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:04.110
we humans would end up spread out
across hundreds of light years of space.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.845
At least we'd give Earth a break,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.915
and allow it to recover
from our mistreatment.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.618
Maybe we don't have to go so far. 

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:15.121
Maybe we could create a new
society on artificial planets

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.090
that we built around the Sun.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.960
But that's a story for another WHAT IF.

